  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q28-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "Expand and simplify the following.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p4-q28-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(1+\\sqrt3)^4+(1-\\sqrt3)^4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$56$\n\nThe surd terms cancel when the two expansions are added.",
          "worked": "Use Pascal’s coefficients $1,4,6,4,1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(1+\\sqrt3)^4&=1+4\\sqrt3+6(\\sqrt3)^2+4(\\sqrt3)^3+(\\sqrt3)^4\\\\(1+\\sqrt3)^4&=28+16\\sqrt3\\\\(1-\\sqrt3)^4&=1-4\\sqrt3+6(\\sqrt3)^2-4(\\sqrt3)^3+(\\sqrt3)^4\\\\(1-\\sqrt3)^4&=28-16\\sqrt3\\\\(1+\\sqrt3)^4+(1-\\sqrt3)^4&=(28+16\\sqrt3)+(28-16\\sqrt3)\\\\(1+\\sqrt3)^4+(1-\\sqrt3)^4&=56\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q28-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(1+\\sqrt3)^4-(1-\\sqrt3)^4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$32\\sqrt3$\n\nSubtract the entire second expansion; the rational terms cancel.",
          "worked": "Use Pascal’s coefficients $1,4,6,4,1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(1+\\sqrt3)^4&=1+4\\sqrt3+6(\\sqrt3)^2+4(\\sqrt3)^3+(\\sqrt3)^4\\\\(1+\\sqrt3)^4&=28+16\\sqrt3\\\\(1-\\sqrt3)^4&=1-4\\sqrt3+6(\\sqrt3)^2-4(\\sqrt3)^3+(\\sqrt3)^4\\\\(1-\\sqrt3)^4&=28-16\\sqrt3\\\\(1+\\sqrt3)^4-(1-\\sqrt3)^4&=(28+16\\sqrt3)-(28-16\\sqrt3)\\\\(1+\\sqrt3)^4-(1-\\sqrt3)^4&=32\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
